    verification dcImplementGate : Test { :>> id = "0d620008-0812-4208-9b3e-000000120008"; :>> title = "Sprint 247 implement gate"; :>> createdAt = "2026-08-12"; :>> createdBy = "claudeOpus5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::demo; :>> procedureText = "Implemented at b518c23. All five blockers delivered + the SE chain + D0129 + 2 processes + 2 skills + 11 Issues. Live-verified: remote merge methods (gh api shows squash=false rebase=false), branch protection (force_push=false deletions=false enforce_admins=true requires_pr=false so the facts lane still works), portable pre-commit runs clean and finds the binary by probing, duplicate-identity guard finds 26 real pre-existing duplicates and grandfathers them, `keel actor` refuses unregistered/binds registered, write path attributes from the binding. clippy clean; 146 tests; validate + guard + check-engine green; CI green at b518c23."; }
    part dcImplementGateR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "0d620009-0812-4209-9b3e-000000120009"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "b518c23"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-12"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus5"; }

    verification dcReviewGate : Test { :>> id = "0d62000a-0812-420a-9b3e-00000012000a"; :>> title = "Sprint 247 review gate"; :>> createdAt = "2026-08-12"; :>> createdBy = "claudeOpus5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "Reviewed. The strongest property of this increment is that nothing was papered over: the duplicate-identity guard immediately found 26 REAL pre-existing violations and they were grandfathered VISIBLY (warnings every run + issue080) rather than suppressed or retro-failed, honouring the issue068 forward-only lesson; and the kernel instance validator's pre-existing failure on 11 committed decisions was recorded as issue081 with the SKIP_VALIDATE bypass stated in the record rather than used silently. The identity control refuses instead of defaulting, which is the correct direction for a security-relevant guard. Two things deliberately NOT done: the frozen-schema marker declarations (needs human sign-off) and the two-lane POLICY being written into CLAUDE.md as in-force (D0129 is proposed — only the mechanical controls are documented as active). Clean."; }
