    verification dcRetroGate : Test { :>> id = "0d62000e-0812-420e-9b3e-00000012000e"; :>> title = "Sprint 247 retro gate (autonomous, D0049)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-08-12"; :>> createdBy = "claudeOpus5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::analyze; :>> procedureText = "Autonomous retro (D0049). WELL: (1) verifying every agent claim against code before writing a requirement on it caught a wrong inference (latest sprint 246, not 163) and let each SR cite file:line — requirements grounded in evidence rather than in a report; (2) the new guard was made FORWARD-ONLY the moment it found pre-existing violations, so the honest-state doctrine held under pressure instead of being traded for a green board; (3) the number-collision defect was proven by EXPERIENCE mid-sprint (below), which is far stronger evidence than the audit alone. AVOIDABLE-ISSUE 1: I piped `git commit` output to `tail`, which hung the kernel JVM for five minutes — CLAUDE.md §6 documents exactly this ('NEVER pipe conda run output'). LESSON: the prohibition applies to any command whose HOOKS invoke conda, not just direct conda calls; redirect to a file instead. AVOIDABLE-ISSUE 2: a bare `cat > file` with no heredoc blocked on stdin for two minutes. LESSON: never emit a redirect without an input source in a non-interactive shell. LIVE CONFIRMATION OF issue074: mid-sprint I allocated issue071 while an earlier uncommitted session had already claimed 071 in two Rust comments; git reported NO conflict because the claims lived in different files, and it surfaced only because a hook told me to read a diff. That is the exact mechanism the guard now catches, and it happened to the engine's own authors within one hour — the strongest possible argument for the control. Resolved on the principle that the MODEL is the register of record and a code comment is not an allocation (mine kept 071, the unfiled defect became issue079). Estimate 8 pts, delivered. Two Issues (080, 081) were raised BY doing the work — both pre-existing debt that had never been visible."; }
    part dcRetroGateR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "0d62000f-0812-420f-9b3e-00000012000f"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "b518c23"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-12"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeOpus5"; }
